/**
 * The camera a host draws a scene with no active camera through — one rule on every host: it
 * stands at `eye`, looks at `target` with +Y up, vertical field of view `yfov` (radians), clip
 * planes `near` / `far`, focus at `focus_distance` (eye → target). A host orbit about `target`
 * starts from this pose: its angles and radius come from eye → target.
 * `orbit_distance` is the level distance along +Z before the lift (shorter than
 * `focus_distance`); hosts read it only as «a framing exists» (> 0, always so here).
